// part-self-update.fk — the body's self-detect-and-update DECISION for a part, as a recipe.
//
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
//
// Self-improvement has two halves: crystallizing a part to NATIVE (Form->asm, no clang) and re-earning
// it champion-challenger gated (never regress); and a content-addressed part-update that converges to
// the same value at every cell, by any gossip path. This recipe is the SEAM between them — the WHEN:
// given a part's local content-address, the mesh's converged content-address for that part, and a
// betterness verdict (champion = the part running now, challenger = the mesh's), decide hold vs update,
// never regress, and settle (no thrash). The fetch is the mesh relay's; the swap is the hot-swap's;
// this is the gate.
//
// A part is identified by its content-address (substrate NodeID — same shape == same address). drift is
// simply a different address. So the whole organism self-updates: a cell improves a part -> its new
// content-address gossips through the mesh -> every body detects the drift, gates it champion-challenger,
// and hot-swaps the native part in. No coordinator; convergence is a property of these recipes.
//
// a part has drifted when the mesh offers a DIFFERENT content-address than the one running now.
section [form.bml] {
    def psu-drifted?(local-addr, mesh-addr) = (Comparable) local-addr == mesh-addr ? 0 : 1;
    // update ONLY when drifted AND the mesh's part wins the champion-challenger gate (challenger-wins=1).
    // same-address -> hold (already current); drifted-but-not-better -> hold (never regress).
    def psu-should-update?(local-addr, mesh-addr, challenger-wins) = (Comparable) psu-drifted?(local-addr, mesh-addr) == 0 ? 0 : (Comparable) challenger-wins == 1 ? 1 : 0;
    // the address running after this pass: the mesh's if we swap, else the one we hold.
    def psu-next-addr(local-addr, mesh-addr, challenger-wins) = (Comparable) psu-should-update?(local-addr, mesh-addr, challenger-wins) == 1 ? mesh-addr : local-addr;
    // settled: a second pass over the result is a no-op — the loop converges, it does not thrash.
    def psu-settled?(local-addr, mesh-addr, challenger-wins) = (Comparable) psu-should-update?(psu-next-addr(local-addr, mesh-addr, challenger-wins), mesh-addr, challenger-wins) == 0 ? 1 : 0;
    0;
}
